# Per-package statement-coverage floors, enforced by `make cover`. Reviewed like code.
#
# Floors ratchet upward only. `make cover-ratchet` raises a floor once measured coverage clears
# it by a whole point; nothing lowers one. A pull request that lowers a floor fails
# `make cover-ratchet-check` unless a commit on the branch carries an anchored
# `coverage-floor-lowered: <package> <reason>` line naming the lowered package.
#
# A floored package that exists but declares no functions yet reports PENDING and passes. Once
# it has code, a missing profile entry is a failure: deleting a package's tests must not
# silently satisfy its floor. PLAN.md section 11 wants no vanity global number, so a package
# earns a line here when its semantics are worth a number.
#
# package                          floor%  note
internal/queue                     90.0    PLAN.md section 11: the pure state machine
internal/store                     85.0    PLAN.md section 11: durability and recovery
internal/subject                   95.0    issue #3: a matcher bug misroutes silently
internal/id                        95.0    issue #3: ids are the spine of messq trace
internal/errs                      95.0    issue #3: the closed sentinel set
internal/clock                     90.0    issue #3: the seam every timing test runs through
internal/docsguard                 95.0    issue #4: the gate that keeps the normative spec honest
